IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`
IMPORT `roc12-schedules-1-3`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore) -- tests for the First, Second and Third Schedules (roc12-schedules-1-3.l4).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the Schedules (lines 7745 to 7784 of the source file) before the run.

§ `First Schedule paragraph 1`
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the relevant date` EQUALS Date 1 4 2022 -- "1 April 2022 (called the relevant date)"
-- Arguments: the kind; the date of commencement or filing; the Court otherwise directs; a written law provides otherwise; the proceedings have been disposed of by the General Division.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a): commenced before 1 April 2022
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order` (Date 31 3 2022) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a): the day before the relevant date
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order` (Date 1 4 2022) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- outside the period the text fixes ("before the relevant date"): (a): commenced on the relevant date, not before it
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order` (Date 15 6 2021) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless the Court otherwise directs"
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "subject to any written law": the written law is outside the sources
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order` (Date 15 6 2021) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the direction is the text's own "unless"
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(b) the subsequent proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court pursuant to a transfer order` (Date 1 6 2023) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b): follows a transfer order in proceedings (a) saves, so no date of its own
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(b) the subsequent proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court pursuant to a transfer order` (Date 1 6 2023) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (b) with a contrary direction
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(c) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in a District Court or a Magistrate's Court` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c): commenced before the relevant date
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(c) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in a District Court or a Magistrate's Court` (Date 15 6 2022) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- outside the period the text fixes ("before the relevant date"): (c): commenced after the relevant date
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(c)(i) an application to the General Division to transfer proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court to the General Division, and the subsequent proceedings there` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c)(i), following (c) proceedings commenced before the relevant date
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(c)(ii) an appeal to the General Division from proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c)(ii)
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(c)(ii) an appeal to the General Division from proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court` (Date 15 6 2022) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- outside the period the text fixes ("before the relevant date"): (c)(ii), following proceedings commenced after the relevant date
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(d) an appeal or originating summons filed in the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (d): filed before the relevant date
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(d) an appeal or originating summons filed in the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division` (Date 15 6 2022) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- outside the period the text fixes ("before the relevant date"): (d): filed after the relevant date
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1 other proceedings` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- proceedings of no kind named in (a) to (d)

-- Fix round, item 3: the periods the text fixes in its own words answer JUST FALSE outside them: "before the relevant date" and "until the disposal of those proceedings by the General Division".
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (a): commenced before the relevant date but disposed of by the General Division: the period "until the disposal" has ended
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a): not yet disposed of
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order` (Date 15 6 2022) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (a): both periods have been left
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(c) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in a District Court or a Magistrate's Court` (Date 15 6 2021) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (c): the disposal bar is (a)'s only, so disposal of the District Court proceedings does not end (c)
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(b) the subsequent proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court pursuant to a transfer order` (Date 1 6 2023) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b): no date of its own and the disposal bar is (a)'s
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(d) an appeal or originating summons filed in the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division` (Date 31 3 2022) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (d): filed on 31 March 2022, the last day before the relevant date
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `sch 1 para 1(d) an appeal or originating summons filed in the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division` (Date 1 4 2022) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- (d): filed on the relevant date, not before it

§ `First Schedule paragraphs 2 and 3`
-- Arguments: proceedings in the lower Court following an appeal; the judgment appealed against was in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings in the lower Court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- both conditions
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings in the lower Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "if the judgment or order ... was given or made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules"
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 2 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings in the lower Court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not proceedings in the lower Court following an appeal
-- Arguments: entered under Order 70, Rule 5 of the revoked Rules; in force immediately before the relevant date.
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 the caveat is deemed to be a caveat against arrest issued under Order 33, Rule 5` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- both conditions
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 the caveat is deemed to be a caveat against arrest issued under Order 33, Rule 5` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not in force immediately before the relevant date
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 the caveat is deemed to be a caveat against arrest issued under Order 33, Rule 5` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not entered under Order 70, Rule 5 of the revoked Rules
#ASSERT `sch 1 para 3 the date of expiry of the caveat` (Date 30 6 2022) EQUALS Date 30 6 2022 -- "the date on which the caveat would have expired but for the revocation"

§ `Second Schedule`
#ASSERT `sch 2 the case is in a category it sets out` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- the Second Schedule is a heading only in this text
#ASSERT `sch 2 the case is in a category it sets out` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING -- likewise
#ASSERT `sch 2 the case is in a category it sets out` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- likewise

§ `Third Schedule`
#ASSERT `sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 item 1 the convention between the United Kingdom and Austria` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- item 1
#ASSERT `sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 item 2 the convention between the United Kingdom and Italy` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- item 2
#ASSERT `sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 item 3 the convention between the United Kingdom and Germany` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- item 3
#ASSERT `sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 item 4 the treaty between Singapore and the People's Republic of China` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- item 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 item 5 the Hague Service Convention of 15 November 1965` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- item 5
#ASSERT `sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 another instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the table is complete: an instrument not among the five is not set out in it (what Order 1, Rule 3(1) "includes" leaves open is the keel function's)
-- The keel function takes the table's answer as its input: an instrument outside the table is a Civil Procedure Convention only if O 1 r 3(1) "includes" it.
#ASSERT `o 1 r 3(1) an instrument is a Civil Procedure Convention` (`sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 item 5 the Hague Service Convention of 15 November 1965`) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- set out in the Third Schedule
#ASSERT `o 1 r 3(1) an instrument is a Civil Procedure Convention` (`sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 another instrument`) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not in the table and not shown to be within "includes": what "includes" leaves open
#ASSERT `o 1 r 3(1) an instrument is a Civil Procedure Convention` (`sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `sch 3 another instrument`) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- not in the table but a convention between different States relating to civil procedure: within "includes"
#ASSERT `sch 3 the Gazette number of the convention` `sch 3 item 1 the convention between the United Kingdom and Austria` EQUALS JUST "T 2/1999" -- item 1
#ASSERT `sch 3 the Gazette number of the convention` `sch 3 item 2 the convention between the United Kingdom and Italy` EQUALS JUST "T 3/1999" -- item 2
#ASSERT `sch 3 the Gazette number of the convention` `sch 3 item 3 the convention between the United Kingdom and Germany` EQUALS JUST "T 4/1999" -- item 3
#ASSERT `sch 3 the Gazette number of the convention` `sch 3 item 4 the treaty between Singapore and the People's Republic of China` EQUALS JUST "T 2/2001" -- item 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 the Gazette number of the convention` `sch 3 item 5 the Hague Service Convention of 15 November 1965` EQUALS JUST "T 1/2023" -- item 5
#ASSERT `sch 3 the Gazette number of the convention` `sch 3 another instrument` EQUALS NOTHING -- no entry
#ASSERT `sch 3 the title of the convention` `sch 3 item 1 the convention between the United Kingdom and Austria` EQUALS JUST "Convention between the United Kingdom and Austria regarding legal proceedings in civil and commercial matters" -- item 1
#ASSERT `sch 3 the title of the convention` `sch 3 item 2 the convention between the United Kingdom and Italy` EQUALS JUST "Convention between the United Kingdom and Italy regarding legal proceedings in civil and commercial matters" -- item 2
#ASSERT `sch 3 the title of the convention` `sch 3 item 3 the convention between the United Kingdom and Germany` EQUALS JUST "Convention between the United Kingdom and Germany regarding legal proceedings in civil and commercial matters" -- item 3
#ASSERT `sch 3 the title of the convention` `sch 3 item 4 the treaty between Singapore and the People's Republic of China` EQUALS JUST "Treaty on Judicial Assistance in civil and commercial matters between the Republic of Singapore and the People’s Republic of China" -- item 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 the title of the convention` `sch 3 item 5 the Hague Service Convention of 15 November 1965` EQUALS JUST "Convention on the Service Abroad of Judicial and Extrajudicial Documents in Civil or Commercial Matters done at The Hague on 15 November 1965" -- item 5
#ASSERT `sch 3 the title of the convention` `sch 3 another instrument` EQUALS NOTHING -- no entry
